tection IaC (`github_branch_protection`, rulesets JSON). 2) Check force-push and deletion are blocked on the source branch. 3) Answer no if `allow_force_pushes: true` or bypass is open to the agent's identity. Answer unknown if protection is set only in repo settings and not in code.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to B12.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"B12\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"B12.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\", \"coverage\": [], \"deviations\": [], \"attempts\": []}],\n \"applicability\": \"absent | present | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\",\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\nagent\nagent/migrations\nagent/migrations/001_init.sql\nagent/requirements.txt\nagent/config\nagent/config/agent.yaml\nagent/config/tools.yaml\nagent/Dockerfile\nagent/k8s\nagent/k8s/deployment.yaml\nagent/k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml\nagent/k8s/admission.yaml\nagent/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\nagent/CODEOWNERS\nagent/.mcp.json\nagent/release\nagent/release/manifest.yaml\nagent/README.md\nagent/.github\nagent/.github/workflows\nagent/.github/workflows/release.yml\nagent/prompts\nagent/prompts/system.md\nagent/src\nagent/src/killswitch.py\nagent/src/gateway_client.py\nagent/src/gateway.py\nagent/src/audit.py\nagent/src/approvals.py\nagent/sr